What you find here is a fully 68020 optimized version of the Magic User
Interface (MUI) version 5.0. It is the direct successor of the well known
MUI 3.8 being developed with full permission by the original author
Stefan Stuntz.

MUI still requires a valid keyfile like its old 3.8 version. Fortunately,
if you have been registered to MUI 3.8 already in the past, all you have
to do is copy over your old "mui.key" file to e.g. 'S:' and reboot your
machine. Afterwards, MUI 5.0 should perfectly recognize your keyfile and
will allow you to change all possible configuration.

If you haven't purchased a MUI keyfile yet, but want to do it now, please
go to http://www.sasg.com/ and/or contact Stefan Stuntz directly as he is
the only officially representative for accepting registrations and
generating valid keyfiles. Please hold back from contacting Hyperion
Entertainment and/or Jens Maus/Stefan Burström directly for asking
on how to register your copy of MUI.

If you should find any bugs in MUI 5.0 which do not occur with earlier
MUI releases then please report them in the MUI bugtracker at
http://muidev.de/newticket. Please provide any detail that might be
important and try to give a step by step instruction how to reproduce the
issue.

June 2016
Thore Böckelmann, Jens Maus
